\beq\label{eq:idual}
\max_{p\in\RR^m,q\in \RR} b^T p - tq,\quad\text{s.t.}~\|A^Tp - \alpha r\|_\infty \le q,~q\ge 0,
\eeq
where  $r\in\RR^n$ is given by
$$r_i = \begin{cases}1,&i\in L,\\
-1,&i\in U,\\
0,&\text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}$$
Therefore, \eqref{eq:idual} has a solution $(p^*,q^*)$ satisfying $b^T p^*- tq^*= 0$.

According to the last constraint of \eqref{eq:idual}, we have $q^*\ge 0$, which we split into two cases:  $q^*=0$ and  $q^*>0$.
\begin{itemize}
\item[i)] If $q^*=0$, we have $A^T p^*=\alpha r$ and $b^T p^*=0$.
\item[ii)] If $q^*>0$, we let $r^*:=p^*/q^*$, which satisfies $b^T r^* =t=  \|x^*\|_1$ and $\|A^Tr^* - \frac{\alpha}{q^*}r\|_\infty \le 1$, or equivalently, $-\vone+\frac{\alpha}{q^*}r\le A^Tr^*  \le \vone+\frac{\alpha}{q^*}r$.
\end{itemize}
